-- title:
--   Level-q automorphisms stabilise primes below a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, an integer $M'\ne 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\xi\in L$ be a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$) and assume (`hK`) that $K=\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}_L$ of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. $K$ is the subfield of $L(\!(t)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of level [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), where `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with $L$ as fraction field and algebraically closed residue field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and with $\xi$ in the image of $A$ in $L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$, $j\ne 0$, whose Laurent expansion (`hj`) is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant. Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$ and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves over $\Omega$ have no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld-chart hypothesis at every supersingular point of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X}:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), with seven clauses, summarised here) requires: for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\mathrm{XFin}=\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` and satisfying the same supersingularity condition as in `hss` with $y'$ in place of $y$, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with maximal ideal of $W$ generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f,u,v\in W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S:=W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the canonical map $C\to$ stalk at $z$: (i) $e$ carries the germ of the image of $a\in A$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ with `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ satisfies $\tau a-a\in y'$ for all $a\in C$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and inducing the identity on $C/y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining the action of $\tau$ on germs through $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$, $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c-1$ a unit when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$; (v) two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h_i$ with $h_i\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, have distinct contractions along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$ as soon as $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as above containing an element $X_0+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a\in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$; and (vii) a Hasse-type clause: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with this element congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W$ not both non-units with $a^qb-ab^q$ in the maximal ideal of $W$ the expression $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\,\cdot\,-a_0)))=\mathrm{mkS}\,h$ for that element.
--
--   Further, a point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$, an element $\varpi_z$, a point $y'$ of $\mathrm{XFin}$ and the associated data (`hϖz`, `hz`, `hy'`, `hss'`) are fixed as in `hArig`, together with `hy'y`: $y'=y$ as ideals of $C$; and one chart witness at $z$ is fixed, namely a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with `hσ₁`, series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and `hf₁` the congruence $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S_1:=W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$, subject to `hW₁`, which is the conjunction of the seven clauses (i)–(vii) above for $W_1,\sigma_1,e_1$ at this $z$ and $y'$.
--
--   Next, an ideal $J$ of $C$ is pinned by `hJ` as the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ for which there exist $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and an automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ with `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ K τ` preserving $C$, such that $J'$ is the contraction along the induced endomorphism of $C$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The $A$-subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ is pinned by `hB` as the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ x\cdot\varpi_t\in J\}$, viewed as an $A$-subalgebra. Finally $\mathcal{W}$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), subject to: `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; and `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $\mathcal{W}$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{W}$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $\mathcal{W}$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $b$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{W}$, and that $f\in K$ lies in $\mathcal{W}$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h$ outside the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{W}$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) requires: for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho\colon B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k_A`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $=k_A[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ whose vanishing locus is the set of elements of $B$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{W}$, which is compatible with $A\to k_A\to\mathrm{CoordRing}$, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism for $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\mathcal{W}$ stable under $\tau$, there is a unit $c$ of $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,c)\mapsto\det g\cdot c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho\circ\tau$ equals the action `hAction` of that element composed with $\rho$, and $c\ne 1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$; that $B$ is stable under every level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is met by the translate under some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and associated $\tau$ of the set of elements of $B$ lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{W}$; that an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such pairs $(\gamma,\tau)$ lie in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{W}$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism for $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau$ preserves $y$ in the sense that $b\in y\Leftrightarrow\tau b\in y$ for all $b\in C$ with $\tau b\in C$, then $\mathcal{W}$ is $\tau$-stable.
--
--   Finally, let $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and let $\tau_0$ be an automorphism of $K$ over $L$ with `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ₀⁻¹ K τ₀`, and assume $\mathcal{W}$ is stable under $\tau_0$, i.e. $f\in\mathcal{W}\Leftrightarrow\tau_0 f\in\mathcal{W}$ for all $f\in K$. Here `IsLevelAutAt L n ζ m N₀ H γ K τ` asserts that for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH N₀ H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ having nonzero Laurent series, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$, and every $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta=\exp(2\pi i/n)$, the product of the $\iota$-image of the Laurent expansion of $\tau x$ with the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma=\begin{pmatrix}\gamma_{00}&\gamma_{01}/m\\ m\gamma_{10}&\gamma_{11}\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $C$ which is prime, contains the image of $\varpi$, and satisfies $\mathfrak{p}\le y$ and $\mathfrak{p}\ne y$, and for every $c\in C$ with $\tau_0c\in C$, one has $c\in\mathfrak{p}$ if and only if the element $\tau_0 c$ of $C$ lies in $\mathfrak{p}$.
--
--   The statement expresses that the level-$q$ part of the decomposition group acts trivially on the primes of the supersingular chart algebra lying strictly below the supersingular maximal ideal $y$ and above the uniformiser, that is, that the $\Gamma(q)$-level automorphisms stabilise every Igusa component through the supersingular point. It is a step in the local analysis of the reduction of the modular curve of level `GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')` at a supersingular point, deduced from the corresponding statement for the special-component valuation rings, and it feeds the counting of branches at the supersingular point used in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_finset_ends_iff_isLocalization_blowupChart_card_eq_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_finset_ends_iff_isLocalization_blowupChart_card_eq_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked).
